<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meppen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meppen is a town in Emsland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where the Hase joins the Ems. It belonged to the Prince-Bishopric of Münster until 1803, when it passed to the Duke of Arenberg, and in 1815 it came under the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, with the dukes keeping rights as mediatised lords. A large weapons-testing range was set up there by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krupp">Krupp</a> company in the 1870s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meppen.jpg" alt="Meppen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Pusch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historia_urbodomo_Meppen_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
